# The hub image builds from the repo root (hub/docker-compose.yml: context ..)
# because it needs :core as well as :hub. Everything else stays out of the
# build context. On the NAS that folder also holds data/, the family's config
# and tokens, owned by the hub's uid and unreadable by the user running the
# build; with it in the context the build died on "can't stat data" before
# compiling anything. On a dev machine the context would otherwise carry .git,
# app/build and the APKs to the daemon for nothing. Guard 13 in scripts/check.*
# holds the shape: a bare * first, then one line per Dockerfile COPY source.
*
!gradlew
!gradlew.bat
!settings.gradle.kts
!build.gradle.kts
!gradle
!core/build.gradle.kts
!core/src
!hub/build.gradle.kts
!hub/src
!hub/docker-entrypoint.sh
!hub/Dockerfile
